          "filename": "Everything Counts RCA exhibition Routemasters, Royal Albert Hall.jpg",
          "caption": "Four Routemaster buses of the Arriva Heritage Fleet, parked up outside the Royal Albert Hall in London. The tape is not the result of an accident, it's there because the four buses have just been used as mobile exhibits for the Everything Counts exhibition, held by the Royal Collage of Art. The installation took place in nearby Exhibition Road from 10am to 6pm, and the buses are now pictured here 45 minutes later outside the hall, presumbaly to be closer to the RCA building, which is out of shot, to the right. From left to right, they are: \nRM2217 (CUV 217C)\nRM1124 (124 CLT)\nRM6 (VLT 6)\nRML901 (WLT 901)",
